{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "def combinations_list(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Finds all possible combinations (power set) of elements from the input list.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_list must be of type list\")\n\n    n = len(input_list)\n    total_combinations = 1 << n\n    result = []\n\n    for m in range(total_combinations):\n        subset = []\n        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n            if (m >> i) & 1:\n                subset.append(input_list[i])\n        result.append(subset)\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/465", "solution": "from typing import Any, Dict\n\ndef drop_empty(input_dict: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Drops items with 'empty' values from the dictionary, returning a new dictionary.\n    'Empty' values are None or objects for which len() returns 0; other non-sized values are retained.\n    \"\"\"\n    def is_empty(value: Any) -> bool:\n        if value is None:\n            return True\n        try:\n            return len(value) == 0\n        except TypeError:\n            return False\n\n    result: Dict[Any, Any] = {}\n    for key, value in input_dict.items():\n        if not is_empty(value):\n            result[key] = value\n    return result"}
